{"kind":"table","sheet":"Results","address":"A1:F17","rows":17,"cols":6,"values":[[null,null,null,null,null,null],["Hong Kong momentum strategy decisions",null,null,null,null,null],["Five-stock weekly test, 2021-04-07 to 2024-12-31",null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null],["Strategy","What it does","Mean rank IC","Sharpe ratio","Keep or drop","Why"],["5-day momentum","Ranks stocks by their past 5-day return and buys the top two weekly.",-0.029467196139421666,-0.26067032929981554,"Drop","Negative IC and Sharpe suggest short-term noise and reversal. Frequent changes also made this the highest-turnover strategy."],["20-day momentum","Ranks stocks by their past 20-day return and buys the top two weekly.",0.0044455688659248704,0.1092091537409715,"Keep","IC and Sharpe were slightly positive. Keep it as a simple baseline, but the edge is weak and needs a full-universe retest."],["60-day momentum","Ranks stocks by their past 60-day return and buys the top two weekly.",-0.008231772668805287,-0.07948896135433471,"Drop","Both IC and Sharpe were negative, so the slower signal did not predict the next week's relative winners."],["10/30-day moving-average momentum","Ranks stocks by how far their 10-day average is above their 30-day average.",-0.011228762354697112,0.19804976588393713,"Keep","It had the best Sharpe and was the only strategy with a positive cumulative return. Its slightly negative IC means it still needs a larger retest."],["20-day risk-adjusted momentum","Ranks 20-day return after dividing it by recent 20-day volatility.",-0.005377954268696111,-0.13325547986575273,"Drop","Volatility scaling did not improve stock ranking. IC and Sharpe stayed negative."],[null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null],["How to read IC",null,null,null,null,null],["IC is the mean weekly Spearman rank correlation between each signal and the five stocks' returns over the following tradable week.",null,null,null,null,null],["Positive is better. Values near zero mean the signal had little consistent ranking power; each strategy has 195 weekly observations.",null,null,null,null,null],["Keep means retain for a larger point-in-time HSI test. It does not mean the strategy is already proven.",null,null,null,null,null]]}
